WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:04.062
That night Sara and Becky ate supper together.

2
00:00:04.102 --> 00:00:08.804
Sara stared at the fire for a long time, looking thoughtful.

3
00:00:08.824 --> 00:00:09.404
"Are you making up a story?"

4
00:00:09.424 --> 00:00:09.664
asked Becky.

5
00:00:09.684 --> 00:00:31.901
"No, I'm thinking about the person who has done all this."

6
00:00:32.462 --> 00:00:33.963
Sara gestured around the room.

7
00:00:33.983 --> 00:00:37.905
"Perhaps he wants to keep his identity secret.

8
00:00:38.865 --> 00:00:41.907
But I do want him to know how happy he's made me."

9
00:00:43.788 --> 00:00:46.229
Suddenly she noticed something new in her room.

10
00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:52.512
It was a box filled with notepaper, envelopes, pen, and ink.

11
00:00:52.532 --> 00:00:55.594
"Oh!" Sara exclaimed.

12
00:00:55.614 --> 00:00:58.776
"Why didn't I think of this earlier?

13
00:01:00.344 --> 00:01:02.025
I can write a thank-you note!"

14
00:01:03.427 --> 00:01:04.748
And she did just that.

15
00:01:06.469 --> 00:01:08.991
The next morning she left the note on her table.

16
00:01:10.912 --> 00:01:12.353
That evening it was gone.

17
00:01:12.373 --> 00:01:14.815
"He found it!"

18
00:01:15.235 --> 00:01:16.316
Sara said to Becky.

19
00:01:17.457 --> 00:01:20.639
Sara felt happy that she'd written to her mysterious friend.

20
00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:26.424
She'd been able to tell him how thankful she was, and how grateful Becky was too.

21
00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:32.971
That night after supper she settled down to read one of her new books to Becky.

22
00:01:33.992 --> 00:01:36.014
Suddenly they both heard something.

23
00:01:36.034 --> 00:01:38.455
"What's that noise?"

24
00:01:39.236 --> 00:01:39.916
asked Becky.

25
00:01:41.317 --> 00:01:45.320
Sara heard it again—a small, scratching sound at the skylight.

26
00:01:46.861 --> 00:01:48.302
Sara opened the skylight.

27
00:01:48.903 --> 00:01:50.804
It was cold and snowing outside.

28
00:01:50.824 --> 00:01:55.628
"It sounds like a cat trying to get in," she said.

29
00:01:56.828 --> 00:02:03.013
It had been snowing all day, and now, crouched in the snow, was a tiny quivering creature.

30
00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:04.954
"Oh, look!"

31
00:02:05.354 --> 00:02:06.095
Sara cried.

32
00:02:06.115 --> 00:02:07.796
"It's the monkey again."

33
00:02:09.417 --> 00:02:10.458
Becky ran over.

34
00:02:10.478 --> 00:02:12.560
"Are you going to let him in, miss?"

35
00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:15.942
"Yes," said Sara happily.

36
00:02:15.962 --> 00:02:17.963
"Come here, little fellow.

37
00:02:18.704 --> 00:02:19.545
I won't hurt you."

38
00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:23.928
She put out a hand, and the monkey leaped into her arms.

39
00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:26.641
Sara hugged the small creature.

40
00:02:26.661 --> 00:02:31.403
"Nice monkey," she said, kissing its odd little head.

41
00:02:31.423 --> 00:02:36.085
"I do love animals, Becky.

42
00:02:36.625 --> 00:02:38.006
I'll let it sleep with me tonight.

43
00:02:39.046 --> 00:02:41.467
Then I'll return it to the sick gentleman tomorrow."

44
00:02:43.268 --> 00:02:47.870
Sara made a little nest for the monkey, and it curled up like a baby and went to

45
00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:51.211
sleep. The next afternoon Mr.

46
00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:52.612
Carrisford had visitors.

47
00:02:54.016 --> 00:02:59.138
Three Carmichael children—Janet, Nora, and Donald—were sitting with him.

48
00:02:59.938 --> 00:03:01.339
They were trying to cheer him up.

49
00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:05.521
Their father was supposed to return from Russia that afternoon.

50
00:03:07.241 --> 00:03:09.662
Mr. Carrisford was very anxious for Mr.

51
00:03:09.702 --> 00:03:10.823
Carmichael to return.

52
00:03:10.843 --> 00:03:15.165
"Let's talk about the lost girl," Janet said.

53
00:03:15.185 --> 00:03:16.985
"Is it true?"

54
00:03:17.606 --> 00:03:18.386
Nora asked.

55
00:03:18.406 --> 00:03:23.068
"Her father gave all his money to a friend to put into diamond mines?

56
00:03:24.296 --> 00:03:27.157
Then the friend ran away because he thought he'd lost the money?"

57
00:03:27.177 --> 00:03:31.058
"But he didn't really lose it," said Janet.

58
00:03:31.078 --> 00:03:33.259
"I feel sorry for the friend."

59
00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:36.580
"Thank you, Janet," said Mr.

60
00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:39.140
Carrisford. "You're very kind."

61
00:03:40.741 --> 00:03:42.561
Donald was making a lot of noise.

62
00:03:45.182 --> 00:03:46.702
Janet scolded him gently.

63
00:03:46.722 --> 00:03:51.784
"When you come to cheer up an ill person, Donald, you should talk quietly."

64
00:03:53.288 --> 00:03:54.529
"I'm going to be quiet!"

65
00:03:55.049 --> 00:03:55.850
Donald shouted.

66
00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:58.792
"We'll all be as quiet as mice!"

67
00:03:58.812 --> 00:04:02.795
"Mice don't sound like that," Janet said.

68
00:04:02.815 --> 00:04:05.376
"It's fine," Mr.

69
00:04:05.436 --> 00:04:06.757
Carrisford reassured her.

70
00:04:06.777 --> 00:04:09.599
"It keeps me from thinking too much."

71
00:04:12.401 --> 00:04:14.983
"Did you hear about the Little Girl Who Is Not a Beggar?"

72
00:04:15.303 --> 00:04:17.124
Donald was talking loudly again.

73
00:04:17.144 --> 00:04:21.107
"She has new clothes and—" "I hear a cab stopping!"

74
00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:22.228
said Janet.

75
00:04:23.144 --> 00:04:24.285
"It must be Papa!"

76
00:04:25.386 --> 00:04:27.648
They ran to the windows to look outside.

77
00:04:27.668 --> 00:04:31.971
"Yes, it's Papa," said Donald.

78
00:04:31.991 --> 00:04:35.234
"But there's no little girl with him."

79
00:04:36.215 --> 00:04:39.257
The three children ran to the door to greet their father.

80
00:04:40.338 --> 00:04:43.120
He told them to play with Ram Dass while he talked to Mr.

81
00:04:43.161 --> 00:04:45.823
Carrisford. Mr.

82
00:04:45.863 --> 00:04:47.624
Carmichael entered the sitting room.

83
00:04:48.765 --> 00:04:52.028
Mr. Carrisford tried to stand up, but he was too weak.

84
00:04:52.896 --> 00:04:54.097
He slumped in his chair.

85
00:04:54.117 --> 00:04:58.398
"Do you have news of the child adopted by the Russian couple?"

86
00:04:58.779 --> 00:04:59.339
he asked.

87
00:04:59.359 --> 00:05:01.960
"Yes," Mr.

88
00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:02.960
Carmichael began.

89
00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:05.281
"She's not the girl we're looking for.

90
00:05:06.182 --> 00:05:08.543
She's much younger than Captain Crewe's daughter.

91
00:05:09.463 --> 00:05:10.863
Her name is Emily Carew."

92
00:05:12.064 --> 00:05:13.865
When he heard this news, Mr.

93
00:05:13.925 --> 00:05:15.525
Carrisford looked miserable.

94
00:05:15.545 --> 00:05:17.346
"Don't worry.

95
00:05:17.586 --> 00:05:19.387
We'll find the girl you're looking for."

96
00:05:20.047 --> 00:05:21.488
Mr. Carmichael took a seat.

97
00:05:22.828 --> 00:05:24.088
"Perhaps we should look in London.

98
00:05:25.049 --> 00:05:26.909
There are plenty of boarding schools here."

99
00:05:26.929 --> 00:05:31.490
"In fact, there's one right next door," Mr.

100
00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:32.451
Carrisford said.

101
00:05:32.471 --> 00:05:36.192
"Remember the poor servant girl Ram Dass told us about?

102
00:05:37.172 --> 00:05:39.192
While you've been away, we've been helping her."

103
00:05:40.853 --> 00:05:42.953
Just then Ram Dass entered the room.

104
00:05:42.973 --> 00:05:45.154
"Sir," he said.

105
00:05:45.174 --> 00:05:48.075
"The girl from next door is here with the monkey."

106
00:05:48.095 --> 00:05:51.156
"I'd like to meet her," said Mr.

107
00:05:52.524 --> 00:05:53.205
Carrisford. "Bring her in."

108
00:05:56.407 --> 00:05:58.848
Sara came into the room carrying the monkey.

109
00:05:58.868 --> 00:06:01.710
"Hello," she said cheerfully.

110
00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:03.452
"Here's your monkey.

111
00:06:03.932 --> 00:06:04.873
It escaped again."

112
00:06:06.634 --> 00:06:09.576
Then she said a few words to Ram Dass in his native language.

113
00:06:10.797 --> 00:06:12.318
Mr. Carrisford and Mr.

114
00:06:12.358 --> 00:06:13.759
Carmichael looked at each other.

115
00:06:13.779 --> 00:06:16.761
"How do you know that language?"

116
00:06:17.261 --> 00:06:17.782
asked Mr.

117
00:06:17.802 --> 00:06:21.044
Carmichael. "Oh, I was born in India."

118
00:06:22.365 --> 00:06:25.577
Mr. Carrisford sat up so suddenly that he startled
